TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and (Gadd) and add the 5th notes as necessary.

TIP:  The strumming pattern is important which is down, down-up-down.

TIP:  For those opening notes (which may or may not transpose), if you form (D) you can pick the open 4th string <d> and then reach up with your index finger to cover the 4th string/2nd fret <e> and then pick the open 3rd string <g> on the way back down to covering the 3rd string to get back to (D).  Easy.

TIP:  In the harmonica bridge there’s a (CaddG) in which you just add your pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret to get that high <g> in there.  You can just play regular (C) as well.
 

